From 9e3b818bf934628da0c8468834475e2d5e8c26d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:17:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] smp: t6050: release a core with its own CPU_START bit

smp_start_cpu() and smp_stop_cpu() write BIT(4 * cluster + core) to
CPU_START +0x4 and +0x0, which assumes clusters of at most four cores.
T6050 has three clusters of six, so from cluster 1 on the bit belongs to
another core: cpu6 (1:0) sets bit 4, cpu4's, and cpu12 (2:0) bit 8,
cpu8's.

On a J716s both registers read 0x3fffe at rest, one bit per secondary
indexed by the ADT cpu-id, and XNU's release sequence sets
BIT(cpu-id) in +0x4 before the cluster's core bit in +0x8 + 4 * cluster.
Use the cpu-id on T6050, as T8142 already does. The +0x8 core bit, the
part that starts the core, is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
---
 src/smp.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/smp.c b/src/smp.c
index ed63e68..48ae0e4 100644
--- a/src/smp.c
+++ b/src/smp.c
@@ -274,8 +274,14 @@ void smp_secondary_prep_el3(void)
 
 static u32 cpu_start_bit(int index, const struct cpu_info *cpu)
 {
-    /* T8142 has six E cores followed by four P cores, not four-core banks. */
-    if (chip_id == T8142)
+    /*
+     * T8142 has six E cores followed by four P cores, not four-core banks. T6050
+     * has three six-core clusters, so 4 * cluster + core names another core from
+     * cluster 1 on (cpu6 = 1:0 would be bit 4, cpu4's). As XNU does, use the ADT
+     * cpu-id: CPU_START +0x0/+0x4 read 0x3fffe at rest on a J716s, one bit per
+     * secondary.
+     */
+    if (chip_id == T8142 || chip_id == T6050)
         return BIT(index);
 
     return BIT(4 * cpu->cluster + cpu->core);
